  "narrative": "The round-1 discovery evidence supports two strong and clinically meaningful dependency associations. MSI-high cells show a large increase in WRN dependency, and TP53-loss cells show a large reduction in USP7 dependency; both 95% intervals are far from zero and well beyond the approximate 10% relative effect scale for these outcomes, so H10 and H11 are accepted as dataset-specific findings. The KRAS, ERBB2, BRAF, ARID1A-SMARCA2, MYC-POLR2A, and MDM2 associations were mostly small and compatible with no clinically meaningful difference. H6 was especially notable because the signed effect was opposite to the anticipated direction by a very large magnitude; the original KEAP1-loss claim that NFE2L2 dependency would be stronger is therefore rejected, while I registered a reversed claim for the observed opposite association. EGFR amplification H3 is borderline: the signed estimate is near the 10% threshold and the interval is almost entirely positive but narrowly includes zero, making this the most useful independent validation target. H1, H4, H8, and H12 are left unresolved because their upper interval bounds still cross a plausible meaningful effect despite non-significant point estimates. No conclusions are drawn about causality or external generalizability; these are associations in the supplied discovery dataset.",
  "research_notes": "Direction convention: dependency scores are signed to the hypothesis direction; positive signed estimates support the registered claim, negative signed estimates oppose it. More negative raw dependency scores mean stronger dependency. Approximate 10% relative threshold maps roughly to 0.02-0.04 dependency-score units for most outcomes, depending on mean absolute dependency score.\n\nAccepted in H10/H11: MSI-high strongly increases WRN dependency; TP53 loss strongly weakens USP7 dependency. H6 showed an unusually large opposite effect, so reverse claim registered.\n\nValidation requested for H3 because EGFR amplification is biologically plausible, the point estimate is near the clinical threshold, and the discovery interval nearly excludes zero. H1/H4/H8/H12 remain unresolved but deferred unless follow-up analyses indicate a clearer signal.\n\nProposed follow-ups: reverse NFE2L2 by KEAP1 loss; EGFR-by-KRAS interaction; SMARCA2 ARID1A-by-SMARCA4 interaction; KRAS dependency in adenocarcinoma subtype."
